EXACT MATHEMATICAL ERRORS FOUND IN STAGE 07a
1. For q=1 and the chosen branch s=i, t=x+iy gives
   Re(st)=Re(i(x+iy))=-y.  The 07a background shading already placed the
   Re(st)>0 colour in the lower half-plane and Re(st)<0 colour in the upper
   half-plane, but the two textual sign/dominance labels were placed on the
   opposite halves.  Thus text, signs, formulas, and colour semantics did not
   agree.
2. The physical, uncut z-plane was shaded and labelled as if e^{S_+} and
   e^{S_-} had sheet-independent dominance regions.  This is false because
   z=t^2 identifies t and -t while S_+(-t)=S_-(t) and S_-(-t)=S_+(t).
   The same physical z therefore receives exchanged exponential labels on the
   two sheets.

CORRECTIONS TO THE FIGURE
- A function dominance_at(t,s) now derives the label from the computed sign of
  Re(s*t), with a tolerance only for detecting the equal-modulus boundary.
- Label samples are constructed normal to the equal-modulus line and passed to
  that function.  Labels are no longer assigned to hard-coded quadrants.
- In the reference t-plane, the lower half-plane is blue and labelled
  Re(st)>0, e^{S_+} dominant; the upper half-plane is orange and labelled
  Re(st)<0, e^{S_-} dominant.
- Panel (a) and all physical-z rotation insets are unshaded.  They contain only
  the mapped rays, the branch point, and explicit annotations that dominance
  requires a sheet/branch choice and t -> -t exchanges S_+ <-> S_-.
- The mapped z conditions remain rays, not full lines: equal modulus at
  theta_eq=-phi and constant phase at theta_phase=pi-phi modulo 2pi.
- Panel (b) retains full straight lines because the conditions are lines on the
  t-cover.  The points t and -t are marked as sheet I and sheet II over the same
  z=t^2, with an arrow between them.

FORMULAS, PARAMETERS, AND BRANCHES
- z=t^2, s^2=-q.
- S_+(t)=2st, S_-(t)=-2st, Delta S=4st.
- Equal modulus: Re(Delta S)=0, equivalently Re(st)=0; dashed and called
  Stokes under the explicitly stated manuscript convention.
- Constant phase: Im(Delta S)=0, equivalently Im(st)=0; solid and called
  anti-Stokes under that convention.
- Re(st)>0: e^{S_+} dominant.  Re(st)<0: e^{S_-} dominant.
- Panels (a),(b): |q|=1, phi=arg(q)=arg(F)=0, chosen s=i with
  arg(s)=(phi+pi)/2.
- Panel (c): |q|=1 and phi in {0, pi/4, pi/2}, in fixed Bargmann z
  coordinates.  For each phi the script uses arg(s)=(phi+pi)/2 for validation;
  the displayed z rays depend only on phi.
- t-plane equal-modulus line direction: pi/2-arg(s).
- t-plane constant-phase line direction: -arg(s).
- Mapping doubles angles and identifies opposite t-rays, giving physical rays
  theta_eq=-phi and theta_phase=pi-phi modulo 2pi.
- Changing s to -s exchanges the sheet/exponential labels but not the physical
  z rays.
- |q| was fixed at 1.  It was not allowed to rotate rays; it changes only
  |s|=sqrt(|q|) and therefore the magnitude of Re(Delta S), i.e. contrast.

TEXT AND CAPTION CHANGES
The note, manuscript paragraph, and caption now state that the exponentials
are single-valued on the t-cover; t and -t lie above the same z but exchange
S_+ and S_-; physical-z dominance requires a sheet/branch choice; and the
ordinary uncut z-plane is not divided into global sheet-independent dominance
regions.  They retain the explicit equal-modulus/constant-phase convention,
the rotation with arg(F)=arg(q), the unitary equivalence
U_chi H(F) U_chi^dagger=H(F exp(i chi)), and the fact that |q| controls
contrast but not angles.  The Hamiltonian normalization V/2 and all physical
parameter names were unchanged.

BIBLIOGRAPHY DIAGNOSIS AND NORMALIZATION
The manuscript uses classic BibTeX with \bibliographystyle{unsrt}.  Inspection
of manuscript.bbl showed that unsrt printed given names exactly as supplied:
entries already using initials were abbreviated, while full `.bib` given names
were rendered in full.  There was no configured global initials option.

The smallest robust correction was therefore to normalize every personal
`author` and `editor` field in manuscript/references.bib individually.  Full
given names were replaced with their existing, directly derivable initials;
no names were invented and no external metadata lookup was needed.  Family
names, particles/compound family names (Olde Daalhuis, El-Jaick, Bonorino
Figueiredo), order, accents in family names, and identities were preserved.
The transliterated given name `Yu.` was retained meaningfully in `S. Yu.
Slavyanov`.  The corporate author `{NIST Digital Library of Mathematical
Functions}` was preserved verbatim and not treated as a personal name.
Translator data and every title, journal, publisher, address, year, volume,
issue, page range, DOI, URL, ISBN, eprint, citation key, and citation order were
left unchanged.

The generated manuscript/manuscript.bbl and rendered bibliography were
inspected in full.  All 26 rendered entries on pages 18--20 use initials only
for personal given names.  The DLMF corporate author remains spelled out.
Personal editors do not happen to be displayed by unsrt for the cited DLMF
misc entry, but their source field was normalized as required.

GENERATION, BIBLIOGRAPHY, AND BUILD COMMANDS
1. MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp/matplotlib-07b PYTHONPATH=src python \
   scripts/07a_stokes_geometry.py
2. bibtex manuscript/manuscript
3. cp manuscript/manuscript.bbl manuscript.bbl
4. latexmk -g -pdf -outdir=manuscript manuscript/manuscript.tex
5. After the final graphical correction:
   MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp/matplotlib-07b PYTHONPATH=src python \
   scripts/07a_stokes_geometry.py
   latexmk -pdf -outdir=manuscript manuscript/manuscript.tex

The explicit BibTeX step was necessary because the first ordinary latexmk run
read a stale root-level ignored manuscript.bbl before latexmk registered the
outdir bibliography dependency.  The generated manuscript/manuscript.bbl was
copied to the location consumed by that first pass, and the forced documented
build then registered and used the outdir bbl.  Final TeX input tracing shows
`(manuscript/manuscript.bbl)`.

